--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

None. The application is a single HTML file built from the sources in this
repository: HTML and CSS written for this project, a translation table with
four locales, a time zone engine and a short list of cities, all in plain
JavaScript. It bundles no library, no framework, no analytics and no font
file, and it loads nothing from the network at runtime - not even a CDN copy
of anything.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Time zone data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

No time zone database is shipped, copied or derived here. Offsets are read at
runtime from the browser's own implementation of Intl.DateTimeFormat, which
follows the IANA time zone database maintained by the browser vendor. This
project does not redistribute that data; it asks the engine that already has
it. That is also why the page stays correct when a government changes its
daylight saving rules: the next browser update carries the change.

"UTC" and the IANA zone identifiers used in the city list (for example
Europe/Belgrade) are identifiers from the public time zone database. Only the
names are used.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Names
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

City and country names are used descriptively to identify places. No
affiliation with any city, country or standards body is claimed or implied.
